{"id": 99, "ts": 1783766027.1823788, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I appreciate the confidence in Candidate\u202fB\u2019s reliability and stress handling, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the stronger overall fit. While B is indeed very conscientious and handles stress well, we have no documented evidence of his decision\u2011quality or attention to detail, and his relatively weak memory for numbers could be a safety risk on long\u2011haul routes where precise data handling is essential. Moreover, his habit of making nasty remarks raises serious crew\u2011cooperation concerns that are harder to remediate than a \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d attitude.\nCandidate\u202fC, on the other hand, demonstrably anticipates dangerous situations and sees complex connections\u2014clear indicators of high\u2011quality decision\u2011making and technical competence. His excellent spatial vision and very good leadership qualities further support his ability to manage the demanding operational environment of international flights. Although he is regarded as a show\u2011off and not very open to new ideas, these attitude issues are less likely to impair safety than a lack of decision\u2011quality or numeric accuracy, and can be addressed through targeted CRM training.\nTherefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC as the best overall match for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
